# Owners of the paths the agent may not write (M2-01).
#
# This is the only one of the three layers that is a real control. The tool-layer deny list
# and the local git hooks are convenience: both live on the machine of the party they
# constrain, and either can be removed by that party in one command. This file is enforced by
# GitHub, server-side, against a branch protection rule the committer cannot edit from a
# branch. Everything else in the protected-paths design is downstream of that one property.
#
# It does nothing on its own. CODEOWNERS is inert until "Require review from Code Owners" is
# switched on for the default branch, which is M2-02 and which cannot be done from a
# repository that has not been pushed. Until then this file is a statement of intent, and
# check-codeowners.py exists so that intent cannot quietly be mistaken for enforcement.
#
# Syntax note: these are gitignore-style patterns, not the fnmatch patterns in
# aios/config.yml. A trailing slash means the directory and everything under it. The mapping
# between the two lists is checked, because two lists of protected paths that drift apart
# leave the gap exactly where nobody is looking.

# --- The grader ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI definitions and the gate scripts they run. An agent that can edit these can edit its own
# examiner, which is the failure the whole protected set exists to prevent.
/.github/                       @NishantRajiitkgp

# CODEOWNERS itself. Without this line the file grants the power to remove itself.
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @NishantRajiitkgp

# --- The rules -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Configuration is where a gate's severity, the deny list and the protected set are declared.
# Editing it is editing every check at once.
/aios/config.yml                @NishantRajiitkgp
/aios/config.schema.yml         @NishantRajiitkgp
/aios/gates.yml                 @NishantRajiitkgp
/aios/ratchets.yml              @NishantRajiitkgp
/aios/demotions.yml             @NishantRajiitkgp

# The CLI and the hook scripts — the implementation of the checks themselves.
/aios/bin/                      @NishantRajiitkgp

# --- The evidence --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests carry the same review weight as the code they cover, and belong in the same pull
# request. What this prevents is not a bad test; it is a passing test amended three weeks
# later to make a failure go away.
/tests/                         @NishantRajiitkgp
*_test.*                        @NishantRajiitkgp
*.test.*                        @NishantRajiitkgp

# Lint, type-check and lockfile configuration. Loosening a linter is indistinguishable in a
# diff from fixing the code it complained about, and lockfiles are where a supply-chain
# substitution arrives.
/requirements.txt               @NishantRajiitkgp
/aios/dependencies.yml          @NishantRajiitkgp
